  internal_calculus controlled host suffix -> Life|Live|Shop|Work territory; unowned host -> independent territory
  internal_calculus path + host -> exact https address; world, audience, and representation select the active Matrix presence
  internal_calculus one parent-bound loopback listener -> N exec-started native workers; each worker opens fresh Matrix/SQLite owner handles and accepts the same transport queue
  source_path cmd/BonfyreWebAddress/src/http_readiness.c
  source_path cmd/BonfyreWebAddress/src/http_readiness.h
  invariant each worker polls up to 64 incomplete HTTP requests and dispatches only complete bounded Content-Length messages; idle sockets and partial headers or bodies cannot occupy the request handler
  invariant request buffers allocate as bytes arrive within the existing 256 KiB whole-request bound; idle connections expire after 10 seconds and incomplete requests after 30 seconds; a full queue refuses its oldest incomplete connection before admitting another
  invariant transport readiness does not run owner handlers concurrently within a worker; the accepted request socket returns to blocking mode and all existing session, namespace and effect checks remain owned by their handlers
  witness cmd/BonfyreWebAddress/tests/http_readiness.test.mjs reproduces idle-connection starvation before the change and checks split framing, incomplete bodies, queue pressure, expiry, malformed-framing refusal and header/body separation
  invariant only /apps/ targets frame against the 640 KiB request capacity; every other target is held to 256 KiB from the moment its request line arrives, so oversized headers or a declared Content-Length it could never accept get 413 at header time instead of holding a connection while the body is awaited
  witness 2026-10-18: http_readiness.test.mjs (7) and week_web.test.mjs framing refusal pass again; both had regressed when the capacity was raised to 640 KiB for /apps/ uploads
  witness packs/no-simulation/http-readiness-20261013/browser.json completes the previously stalled four-territory intake-to-Studio browser flow at desktop and phone widths with one native worker
  forbidden_inference a bounded request-readiness queue -> parallel owner execution, completed authorization, production capacity or bounded response-write latency
  invariant CMS form text uses the shared Lex JSON emitter to preserve admitted tabs, carriage returns, newlines, quotes, backslashes and UTF-8; escaping that exceeds the bounded JSON carrier refuses before invoking the native store
  invariant CMS form admission and complete edit rendering share a 64 KiB decoded-field bound including the terminator; HTML escaping has capacity for every admitted field and the complete 128 KiB JSON carrier
  witness cmd/BonfyreWebAddress/tests/cms_editor_journey.test.mjs round-trips a 65535-byte escape-heavy field through native save, Chrome editing and reload; decoded UTF-8 and 256 KiB request overflows retain the previous record
  forbidden_inference A decoded field below 64 KiB -> an unlimited form or transport request; total native JSON and HTTP envelopes remain independently bounded
  witness cmd/BonfyreWebAddress/tests/week_web.test.mjs saves a complete tabbed preparation plan from Chrome through native CMS, checks private Desk access, round-trips control characters and refuses escaping expansion beyond the carrier bound without creating a record
  forbidden_inference a saved preparation draft -> publication, a food safety determination, a purchase or a booked helper
  invariant the note room sizes its content and HTML response from the selected CMS body rather than truncating it at a fixed display buffer; authored line breaks remain visible and long text wraps within the viewport
  witness cmd/BonfyreWebAddress/tests/week_web.test.mjs opens the saved preparation plan in Chrome at phone width, compares the reader text with the stored snapshot, reads a 64 KB field with extensive HTML escaping in full and checks direct-read denial for another account and a guest
  internal_calculus a root HTML response injects only the same native resolved subject, presence, territory, world, audience, and canonical address into the reusable Matrix visual grammar; it never guesses a subject from hostname styling
  internal_calculus an addressed root or bounded local subject path compiles the same native Matrix cut into RO-Crate JSON-LD and a virtual Zarr v3 group; an independent owner may attach an immutable digest-and-receipt reference for that exact active Presence, but its body/state/authority stays with the owner and both machine carriers still begin with one resolve
  internal_calculus Accept negotiation selects API, MCP, A2A, or BonfyreFS only when a matching Matrix presence exists; HTML remains an ordinary browser surface
  internal_calculus a host standing in front of a territory apex is a subject address: its own published SiteProgram composes it, and a published subject program is tried before the territory's composed front page so a member's address carries their surfaces rather than the territory's reading
  internal_calculus a subject host with no fabric bundle composes nothing rather than falling back to the territory's sources; the hour's phase still orders a subject page but the subject, not the phase, names it
  internal_calculus a static publication writes each subject host under hosts/<host>/ and the edge worker resolves that prefix before the shared estate, so one published tree answers every address without copying itself under each of them
  internal_calculus the machine aperture answers JSON-RPC at /mcp from the edge, over objects this estate has already published, because the adapter it used to tunnel to needed a host that no longer exists
  internal_calculus an aperture with no session and no owner behind it is read-only by construction; an effect tool is refused by name with the reason rather than being absent, so a caller learns the boundary instead of a silence
  source_path integrations/mcp/bonfyre_mcp_2026_adapter.mjs
  witness 2026-09-25 /mcp on aurekai.work answered initialize as bonfyre-edge-aperture at protocol 2025-06-18, listed estate_search, estate_page and estate_boundary, returned real retained material for a search, and refused media_transport_lease as an effect the edge holds no authority to grant
  witness 2026-09-25 the break was six worker routes carrying a null script -- aurekai.work/mcp*, /oauth*, /.well-known/oauth-*, and three subdomains -- left from the dead Oracle tunnel. A scriptless route bypasses the worker to an origin that no longer answers, so every one of those paths returned 522 while the rest of the estate served normally; deleting them restored them to the estate worker
  known_gap no authorization server stands behind the aperture and /.well-known/oauth-protected-resource says so with an empty list, because advertising one that cannot complete a flow sends a connector into a dead end. A connector needing OAuth still cannot attach
  internal_calculus the public directories and the addresses are the same fact read twice: an institution row carries its own address when this estate has published a presentation for it, and the people surface lists the members standing in the territory; an address is never guessed from a hostname that has no published presentation
  internal_calculus the native project MCP uses the exact Streamable HTTP POST /mcp contract through the edge; OAuth PKCE exchanges a BonfyreAuth-backed session at the authority bridge, which requires read scope for bounded discovery/read methods and write scope for unknown or mutating tool calls before forwarding to the MCP owner
  internal_calculus an OAuth MCP session with a current institution closure but no Bonfyre admin closure receives a freshly compiled institutional tool slice: closure coordinates, namespace-scoped CMS read/create, private ForeignTwin observation, and bounded Upper90 review work; a self-scoped actor with no institutional closure receives a different actor-local slice for its own carrier recipes and private ForeignTwin observation; only current bonfyre/admin reaches the full project MCP owner and its additive canonical BonfyreAuth user/tier/active/grant controls plus schema-bound BonfyreCMS copy controls
  internal_calculus the MCP transport also exposes canonical owner-backed resources, bounded architecture resource templates, and tool-grounded prompts; these are read/preparation carriers and do not create a second institutional store or effect authority
  internal_calculus MCP can resolve a host/path/world/audience/representation through the configured local Matrix store or the declared Oracle native BonfyreWebAddress read route and read a subject constellation; the remote route permits only native resolve/constellation with fixed binary/database coordinates, while an absent shared Matrix store is reported as unconfigured rather than bootstrapped as a demo estate
  internal_calculus authenticated CMS HTMX fragments derive navigation and field grammar from the native CMS registry after compiling the session closure: an ordinary self account sees only physical_carrier, a generic write session sees registered grammar, and a previously admitted private Upper90 namespace sees only grammar under that private closure; create and update invoke BonfyreCMS by fork/exec with the resulting isolated namespace
  internal_calculus the controlled Work root also compiles one Bonfyre/admin-only private repair room: it rechecks the live named admin admission before rendering canonical user/tier/activity, session-revoke, and institution grant/revoke forms, links to schema-bound native CMS copy, and calls BonfyreAuth by fixed argv only; any tier/activity change burns stale sessions before the next login compiles a new scope, and no delegated estate or self closure can route to this room
  internal_calculus an ordinary authenticated account may compile only an actor-owned PersonalProfile in the Life/self territory, retain its isolated PhysicalCarrier recipe, and observe a public source only into its actor-derived private ForeignTwin root; generic Matrix publication, market work, institutional/Frappe records, public ForeignTwin projection, finance, and external effects still require their separate write/authority owners
  internal_calculus static territory paths for login, signup, logout, account, saved material, Studio and CMS are not interpreted by the Worker. A broad static route preserves their path/query while redirecting to auth.aurekai.life, auth.aurekai.live, auth.aurekai.shop or signin.aurekai.work; the exact territory apex can instead lower directly to the same native/Tunnel origin when the Worker cannot serve its request budget. Native WebAddress serves progressive forms and same-origin account/session requests in either transport realization. The native account composes saved material, self-presence/self-ForeignTwin controls and declared outside-account relationships from their existing owners rather than creating a parallel member dashboard store
  internal_calculus an actor-owned self Presence remains addressable but its HTML, RO-Crate, and Zarr carrier resolution rechecks the live session actor prefix; public/market actor publication and institutional Life roots retain their separately declared visibility
  internal_calculus before a PhysicalCarrier recipe is retained, its governed HTTPS address is resolved through the current Matrix AddressPlane cut; a self-scoped actor must resolve to its own actor-owned subject while generic/private closures retain their independently admitted namespace policy
  internal_calculus a CMS request on an admitted Upper90, JRSS, AI Loss, or Leads host first obtains the current native Upper90 closure; its first exact scope compiles a private estate namespace, and only then may the ordinary CMS HTMX owner render or save declared grammar
  internal_calculus a private /studio address is compiled from that same fresh estate/scope closure into a bounded human workroom: native Upper90 review work plus links to the independently closure-derived CMS and ForeignTwin carriers, never the global Aurekai Studio
  internal_calculus exact delegated hosts Upper90, JRSS, AI Loss, and Leads carry a fixed host-to-institution selector to BonfyreAuth; native admission evaluates the current institution role on every request and selects read versus write from the original request method
  internal_calculus after exact institutional admission, the native Upper90 product dispatcher resolves auth-user identity to an AuthorityGraph-backed named role and scope, renders only that HTML closure, and converts a bounded opaque-reference request into an upper90-private WorkGraph review mission
  internal_calculus delegated client hosts decline public HTTP redirects and all generic discovery, feed, RO-Crate, Zarr, federation, protocol, commerce, and sitemap carriers until a client-specific AuthorityGraph envelope names a lawful private carrier
  internal_calculus internet.aurekai.work resolves one public Work-territory Matrix institution; its root and typed maintained path cuts compile through the same WebAddress resolution and RO-Crate/Zarr closure as every other bound subject, while its authenticated Operator Lab retains source/index results only as receipt-bound CandidateAddress state for later ForeignTwin admission
  internal_calculus an exact protected host -> fixed institution selector -> native BonfyreAuth institution-grant check; GET/HEAD require read and any other original verb requires write, while revocation is checked against the current grant rather than captured in the session
  internal_calculus /.well-known/bonfyre publishes carrier coordinates for Web, API, MCP, A2A, BonfyreFS, CMS, and Habitat without manufacturing semantic objects
  invariant Nginx provides TLS, host forwarding, WebSocket/stream forwarding, and lawful transport concerns only
  invariant edge worker multiplicity changes only transport capacity: each worker recompiles the same request against its own fresh native owner connections, so a process pool cannot become a cache of actor, authority, disclosure, Matrix, or effect state
  invariant the compiler cannot infer a readable private closure, effect authority, claim, or publication from a URL
  invariant a root HTML carrier preserves the exact Matrix resolve result that selected its presence; a reusable static grammar cannot replace that resolved subject with a generic brand or host-derived identity
  invariant RO-Crate and Zarr root routes are generated from current Matrix resolution rather than stored host catalogs; every non-Matrix plane is either explicitly unresolved or names a digest-and-receipt owner reference for the exact resolved Presence instead of fabricating a body
  invariant each owned territory host carries its own document identity: title, description, Open Graph pair and self-referential canonical are emitted from the resolved audience and canonical address, so no owned host declares another host as its canonical and a fetcher that executes no script can still tell the four territories apart
  invariant the A2A agent card and the /a2a endpoint are rendered from one skill table, so a skill cannot be advertised by the card and absent from the endpoint the card names
  invariant representation follows an explicit ask in both directions: a surface holding both forms serves the JSON one to a client that names application/json and the page to a browser, while a client that names neither keeps the representation it already had, so adding negotiation never rewrites what an existing plain fetch reads
  invariant a human-facing machine surface answers a browser with a page and a machine with JSON from one page grammar and one price lookup; the capability catalogue and the A2A carrier render the same number in both representations, so a reader and a crawler are never shown different prices
  invariant every commerce grammar renders one settlement declaration rather than asserting its own: the rail, its quote path and its discovery path are single constants that the x402, MPP, UCP, ACP and Beckn projections each render into their own vocabulary, so five carriers cannot drift into disagreeing about where payment settles, and a carrier that quotes an amount always also declares how it would be paid
  invariant the A2A and x402 carriers quote one capability from one finance service book; the agent-to-agent carrier cannot name a price the payment carrier would not, and an unpriced capability is refused rather than treated as free
  invariant a path-qualified machine closure is accepted only as a bounded path on the request's already-controlled Host; the edge never dereferences or imports a foreign URL supplied as a crate selector
  invariant the discovery descriptor advertises a surface if and only if the organ serves content for it; one predicate over SITE_ROOT/surfaces/<name>.json decides both advertising and serving, so the descriptor cannot name a surface that would 404
  invariant a surface is served only for a host that resolves in the matrix; an unknown host receives 404 even when the surface file exists
  invariant a delegated client host never becomes publicly crawlable or machine-discoverable because a generic public carrier was added elsewhere in Nginx
  invariant an Internet Observatory CandidateAddress is source/query receipt state at discovery_only; the public maintained cut reports only derived membership/counts, and a candidate never fetches, becomes a ForeignTwin, asserts origin liveness, publishes a tool, or grants authority through the WebAddress carrier
  invariant delegated host admission is exact and revocable: an authenticated account must hold a current grant for the same named estate, and a mutation additionally needs the estate write role
  invariant protected delegated hosts use the native private product dispatcher exclusively; an unknown private path cannot fall through to a legacy client application with weaker role semantics
  witness cmd/BonfyreWebAddress/tests/a2a_surface_test.sh proves /a2a, /capability and /protocols each answer a browser with a page carrying the shared stylesheet and topbar and a machine with JSON, and that every capability's priced/unpriced state on the page matches the JSON carrier exactly
  witness cmd/BonfyreWebAddress/tests/a2a_surface_test.sh proves /agents, /market, /property and /sources hand a JSON-asking client JSON and a browser a page, that the root answers an explicit JSON ask with its address descriptor, and that a wildcard or absent Accept still receives exactly the representation it received before negotiation existed
  forbidden_inference an advertised A2A skill, or a quote returned inside a JSON-RPC error -> an agreement to perform that skill for any particular requester, a settled payment, or an invoice
  witness cmd/BonfyreWebAddress/tests/a2a_surface_test.sh proves the endpoint the agent card names answers as application/a2a+json, that every advertised skill is described by both the card and the endpoint, that an unknown skill, an unsupported method, a request with no method and a skill that is not a priced query are each refused with a typed JSON-RPC code rather than a generic 404, and that the sibling /a2a/agent.json and /a2a/resources routes are not swallowed by the new handler
  witness cmd/BonfyreWebAddress/tests/a2a_surface_test.sh proves each of the four owned hosts serves a distinct title, is canonical to itself, and carries exactly one of each identity tag, while still carrying its own resolved Matrix subject and audience
  forbidden_inference a served surface -> authority to invoke, read, or act on anything it lists
  forbidden_inference a public MCP URL -> anonymous project access or authority to invoke a project tool
  forbidden_inference a valid session, paid tier, or JRSS grant -> read or write authority for a different delegated client host
  forbidden_inference an OAuth access token -> authority beyond its verified write scope or bypass of an MCP tool's own effect boundary
  invariant the auth surface holds no credentials: signup, login, logout and account forward to BonfyreAuth, which owns users, sessions and PBKDF2-HMAC-SHA256 at 120000 iterations
  invariant signup and login are progressive forms, not JavaScript-only decoration: a no-script registration creates no session and redirects to the sign-in boundary, while a no-script login forwards the same form values to BonfyreAuth and only then receives the scoped HttpOnly cookie
  invariant a successful browser login may set a Secure HttpOnly SameSite=Lax session cookie only for the controlled parent zone of the request's own Life, Live, Shop, or Work territory; it is revalidated by BonfyreAuth on every request and is never an institution, role, evidence, or effect grant. A browser cookie never crosses sibling territories; cross-territory continuation requires an explicit future authorization exchange
  invariant the auth child is spawned with fork and execv and never through a shell, and a bearer token is validated against its exact shape before it is passed as an argument
  invariant a request body may carry a credential, so no body is logged and no failure response returns a token, a hash, or a salt
  invariant the four exact native member-session hosts may serve checked-in client assets needed by their native account forms; a wildcard host that has no AddressPlane domain and is not one of those four remains refused rather than gaining estate assets by suffix
  invariant Upper90, JRSS, AI Loss, and Leads hosts are dedicated private apertures: they cannot fall through the public Matrix/legacy route, emit noindex/no-store/no-referrer policy on success and refusal, suppress edge access logging, and deny public protocol/machine-discovery path families
  invariant auth is advertised only when the auth binary is executable, on the same terms as a file-backed surface
  invariant the CMS edge accepts only registered native types and declared editable columns; it neither invents a browser schema nor accepts arbitrary SQL columns
  invariant a free self session cannot enumerate or render institutional/Frappe CMS grammar merely because the native registry contains it; private-estate CMS remains available only after its independently checked Upper90 namespace closure is present
  invariant a delegated CMS namespace is derived afresh from the host-selected estate and Upper90 closure for every request; it is never supplied by a URL, form field, session cache, generic actor namespace, or a prior request's process state
  invariant multiple delegated scopes are not silently unioned into one CMS write bucket; the carrier keeps one owner-returned scope closure until an explicit future Room selection is itself admitted
  invariant a delegated private Studio may compose only named owner planes whose inputs are freshly derived from the same admitted estate/scope closure; it cannot borrow global finance, model, Fleming, Frappe, or generic Studio state merely because the browser requested /studio
  invariant a successful CMS save is not publication, anonymous readability, a Frappe write-back, a resolved relation, financial settlement, or external effect
  invariant free self-authoring is exact and non-escalating: it is limited to actor-owned PersonalProfile/self publication at aurekai.life, physical_carrier rows in that actor's isolated CMS namespace, and public-source ForeignTwin observation into that same actor's private root; it cannot select another territory, subject, namespace, actor, institution, public ForeignTwin projection, provider, payment, device, or effect closure
  invariant an actor-owned self Presence is not anonymously scrapeable through its web, RO-Crate, or Zarr address; a missing or different actor receives an indistinguishable no-store/noindex miss, while a self scope on an institutional root does not incorrectly make that institution private
  invariant a PhysicalCarrier recipe cannot retain a foreign, query-selected, fragment-selected, port-selected, stale, or unresolvable URL-shaped value as its subject address; carrier save begins from one current controlled Matrix address resolution, not browser text alone
  invariant an MCP resource or prompt is resolved from the current native owner at read time; it cannot be mistaken for a durable copy, evidence promotion, authorization grant, or effect receipt
  invariant an MCP Matrix address result is only a native AddressPlane cut; actor/session, delegation, information policy, evidence, provider, resource, financial, and effect closures remain independently unresolved unless their owners are separately consulted
  invariant the MCP remote Matrix route carries no shell string or caller-selected database/path; it may invoke only the declared native read contract over the configured owner route
  invariant OAuth scope narrows transport admission by declared MCP method/tool class, while every forwarded tool still enforces its own native authority and effect boundary; unknown or malformed requests take the write path
  invariant a write-scoped Bonfyre session can satisfy a read-only MCP call, and a self-scoped session can be transport-admitted only to its fixed self MCP slice; generic OAuth read/write scope alone cannot select the full project MCP, a delegated institution, or an actor-local slice other than the verified actor
  invariant an institutional MCP tool re-evaluates its caller's live estate/scope closure before each owner invocation; caller-provided estate values can narrow only to an estate already in that closure
  invariant only a freshly verified bonfyre/admin closure may receive the additive administrative MCP tools; they invoke BonfyreAuth or BonfyreCMS directly, never expose password hashes, salts, or session credentials, and do not turn account tier, institution admission, or CMS copy into object/provider/payment/effect authority
  invariant the Bonfyre/admin browser repair room is private/no-store/noindex and available only at the controlled Work root after live named-admin revalidation; its forms may mutate only canonical BonfyreAuth tier/activity/institution admission state, while copy remains in the native schema-bound CMS surface
  forbidden_inference a valid session -> authority for any scope beyond the one the session carries
  forbidden_inference a CandidateAddress retained through the Internet Operator Lab -> a ForeignTwin observation, live service, protocol validation, relationship, callable tool, payment route, or effect authority
  forbidden_inference generic account tier or write scope -> an institution-specific read/write closure
