  known_gap Until 2026-08-29 discovery() emitted api, mcp, a2a, cms and habitat unconditionally for every host while all five answered 404 in production. That is this organ's own forbidden inference -- discovery metadata claiming a named resource is publicly readable -- shipped and served. The prior witness asserted the mcp URL was always present, so the test encoded the defect rather than catching it. Fixed by deriving liveness from the filesystem and serving the surfaces from this organ. API, MCP and A2A are backed by real content; authenticated CMS HTMX fragments are now backed by BonfyreCMS but still are not a public CMS carrier declaration because a valid session and an executable native CMS owner are required. Habitat remains deliberately unbacked. Writing placeholder content would recreate the defect.
  invariant Cloudflare Tunnel and Nginx forward controlled host traffic but terminate unmatched hostnames instead of becoming fallback semantic routers
  invariant a scoped native-organ release stages every compiled source input, including generated native headers, and attests the staged tree before the origin builds; a new executor may never link against an unstaged previous-generation lowering
  invariant native-organ release stages and digests the bounded libbonfyre header set before remote build, so a shared header added by a cross-owner refactor cannot be silently supplied by an older origin checkout
  invariant a configured SQLite location is a literal filesystem path; read-only opens never interpret '?' or '#' as URI query or fragment, and the remaining compatibility URI callers percent-encode those bytes at one bounded boundary
