  witness 2026-09-19 a hostname this estate has published no presentation for returns 404 at the edge rather than the territory's front page, while the estate's shared surfaces and assets still answer at every address
  known_gap Workers custom domains cap at 100 per account, so per-host binding cannot carry an estate that addresses 28,000 publishers; the wildcard route is the only mechanism that scales and the 100 custom domains bound during the cutover were withdrawn once it was in place
  invariant full-estate publisher-address and member-world projections wait through a bounded sixty-second SQLite writer window before refusing, and commit only complete idempotent prefixes (fifty addressed publishers, the publication corpus/collections, or one member surface) instead of holding the estate writer through unrelated work; waiting and committing are scheduling recovery only and never treat a blocked write as an admitted address, owner row, or completed publication
  witness 2026-09-19 1,103 subject hosts answered in aurekai.life -- 893 publishers addressed from retained material rather than ledger bookkeeping -- and aurekai.live, .work and .shop each served their own composition instead of .life's front page, which all three had been serving verbatim as Pages custom domains
