  source_path scripts/deploy_organ.sh
  witness 2026-09-26 every composed subject room was unreadable in a browser and nobody had noticed, because the tests fetch with curl. When a client offered gzip the wire layer packed the body and appended its own Content-Length while the room's original stayed in the buffer; two of them is a malformed response, curl tolerates it and Chrome refuses the page outright with ERR_RESPONSE_HEADERS_MULTIPLE_CONTENT_LENGTH. The stale line is now dropped rather than the new one appended beside it, and the same request returns one Content-Length
  known_gap the assets a room dresses in are served only for a host the matrix admits as a domain, so a room fetched at 127.0.0.1 renders unstyled with no organ layer. That is the gate working, but it means no test that uses a bare address exercises the page a reader actually gets
  internal_calculus how long the edge may keep a thing depends on what kind of thing it is. A URL carrying a content stamp cannot change without the URL changing, so it is immutable; the catalogue is a publication pass and may be an hour stale while it revalidates; a composed page is what actually moves and keeps a short window
  known_gap this estate took itself off the air. Every publish in a working session called purge_everything on all four zones, each purge threw away the whole edge cache, and the next read re-fetched the pages, the catalogue parquets and a 33 MB WebAssembly engine from the object store. Forty publishes in a day put the account past its request budget and all four territories answered HTTP 429. scripts/estate_purge.sh now purges the files that changed, and the cache policy is tiered so the large immutable things are not re-fetched every five minutes
  forbidden_inference a purge being cheap -> a purge being free; the cost is paid by every reader who arrives next and by the account's request budget
