  witness scripts/tests/cloudflare-entrypoints.test.mjs proves the default purge shell reaches the shared Bun owner without Python; empty or mixed full-purge arguments are refused and all exact zones resolve before writes. Mock acceptance is not a live cache freshness witness.
  internal_calculus a caller that asked in JSON is refused in JSON. Every refusal this edge makes -- no page, wrong method -- carried a sentence written for a person, so anything automated reading this estate got prose where it needed a reason it could branch on. A path under a machine surface counts as a machine's question even when the caller forgot to say so
  witness 2026-09-25 measured on all four territories: a machine asking /studio/v1/profile with Accept: application/json received text/html and a sentence; it now receives application/json with an error code, the reason, the address, and what the refusal does not imply
  witness 2026-09-25 aurekai.life answered HTTP 200 to every address on the territory, including addresses that do not exist, because a Cloudflare Pages project held the apex as a custom domain and a Pages custom domain outranks a Workers route. /press, /edition, /archive, /field and /mcp were all unreachable on that territory and every wrong URL was a soft 200. Removing the two custom domains restored the whole territory to the estate; verified afterwards that the apex serves its composed page, the four surfaces answer, an unknown address is a real 404, and the aperture lists its three read tools
  known_gap a Pages custom domain silently outranking a Workers route is not visible from the route table, which listed the worker as the handler for a hostname it never saw. Nothing in this estate checks that the thing answering a territory is the thing declared to answer it
  known_gap the prototype that had been serving that apex carried six sections the composer does not build -- Listen, Watch, Around Fort Worth and Dallas, Discover, Boards, On this day -- and is kept at evidence/origins/tonight-pages-prototype/ as evidence of what was served, not as a page to serve again
  known_gap a Pages custom domain outranks a worker route on the same hostname, so a territory cannot be moved to the worker without first withdrawing it from the Pages project; aurekai.life remains on Pages by the operator's choice
  known_gap a writer that remains blocked beyond the bounded wait is still recorded as refused; the standing publisher does not yet enqueue a durable retry generation for those sidecars
  known_gap 2026-10-12 a member front page's own /w/<world>/<page> links are now followed by scripts/export_subject_hosts.sh (at most 24 per host); before that every such link answered 404 at the edge. The donor stylesheets those pages load were uploaded to the object store by hand that day; scripts/export_static_estate.sh now lists them with the bar, site-program and own-site sheets, and no publish pass has run with that list yet
  witness 2026-10-12 cmd/BonfyreWebAddress/tests/site_product_test.sh sets a site's footer line with site set --footnote, reads it on the front and contact pages, refuses a link that is not https, and clears it with --no-footnote
  known_gap a cleared footer line is a newer record of kind 'cleared', not a deletion; older lines stay in the store and nothing prunes them
  known_gap 2026-10-12 the stylesheet link for independent sites carries a version (?v=5) so the edge cannot hold an old sheet for hours; the number is bumped by hand and nothing derives it from the file
  known_gap 2026-10-12 the edge Worker aurekai-estate receives about 125,000 requests a day at a steady 8,000 an hour (Cloudflare workersInvocationsAdaptive, 2026-10-09 to 2026-10-12) against a free-plan cap of 100,000, so every subdomain answers 429 from about 16:00 UTC until midnight UTC, every day. The apexes and the hosts with their own no-Worker route are unaffected. Who sends the traffic is not known: the stored token cannot read zone analytics
  witness 2026-10-12 docs.aurekai.work answered 429 from the Worker at 16:20 UTC and 200 after it was attached to the Pages project aurekai, whose pages.dev name the zone's wildcard record already targets; a Pages custom domain outranks the Worker route, so the guides no longer pass through the Worker or its daily cap. The project's previous deployment (the September prototype, 4ea24053) is the rollback point
  known_gap 2026-10-12 three Pages projects staged for the shop sites (aurekai-tallgrass, -fernhollow, -juniper) were removed the same day once the bucket route worked; only the guides use Pages
  known_gap the guides now live in two places, the object store and the Pages project aurekai; scripts/publish_estate.sh updates only the first, so a guide changed without running scripts/publish_site_to_pages.mjs is stale at its public address
  witness 2026-10-12 nick.aurekai.life answered 429 from the Worker and 200 at 17:55 UTC after scripts/route_host_through_tunnel.sh gave it its own tunnel record and a no-Worker route, the arrangement the territory apexes already use; it is now composed live by this machine and is down when this machine is
  known_gap 2026-10-12 a tunnel login certificate is bound to one zone; the one held is for aurekai.life, so the three sample shop sites in aurekai.shop could not be routed the same way, and a first attempt left a stray record tallgrass.aurekai.shop.aurekai.life that the held credentials cannot delete
